From d2ac8d547f15ec1207969ca253f6eb0eadaee43a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PowOS <mats@powback.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:05:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: touches go to windows that take them, the
 task's size wins

A touch in a window task went to any window the task draws whose frame
was under the finger. Now it is picked as KWin's own input picks: in
stacking order, shown, painted, not see-through, and its input region
(hitTest: an X window's shape) under the finger; else the task's window.

A window that resizes itself while its task is live (an X client's own
configure: Steam came back at 1659x1746 in a 1351 px wide task) is sized
back to the task, up to five times in a row; one that keeps its own size
is logged with its min size. Touches that don't go to the task's window,
and the windows a task also draws, are logged.
---
 src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp | 103 +++++++++++++++++++--
 src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h   |   7 ++
 2 files changed, 100 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
index 09c6b20..e288b3a 100644
--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
